reaction  to what has gone viral on social media  this evening and that's the video of a  woman going inside a russian news studio  during a live news broadcast going  behind the anchor with a poster  protesting the war saying no war i mean  the fact that she was able to do that is  amazing in russia  what's your reaction  well it's astonishing that she was able  to to do that but i think uh what i was  just reading also that the newspaper  novaya gazietta which is one of the very  very last independent media working in  russia reported on this incident but had  to black out  what the protester was saying because  they're not able to use the necessary  words to actually cover this incident  they're not able to say war or invasion  and i don't know if people understand  the level of censorship that is  happening in russia at the moment not  only obviously our protests being  violently suppressed but nearly all  independent media have been forced out  of the country  closed hundreds of journalists have left  the country over the past  few weeks and again authorities are  using sort of orwellian language to  describe this operation  and bring the hammer down on any  journalists or media who dared to report  what is actually happening in ukraine as  a war or an invasion and we fear that  this censorship which is unprecedented  in russia since the fall of the soviet  union  is only going to increase things look  very serious and very negative in russia  at the moment and we can assume with a  high degree of certainty that the woman  the protester who held up that  sign in the  russian news broadcast she's going to  prison isn't she  obviously very likely very possible um  we've seen  as i'm sure you have as well shocking  videos of people on the street even one  i've seen you know holding a sign that  said nothing a blank sign  and you know immediately being taken  away by security forces you know we  understand that these protesters face a  sort of different fate some are  released immediately with warnings  others may be held for longer periods of  time but the strategy of the authorities  is fairly clear here it's a shutdown  immediately  any type of  any type of critical gestures in public  with violent force to prevent this from  turning into a wider movement which is  also the explanation for this violent  crackdown so that people inside russia  don't see the images of what is actually  happening in ukraine the kremlin  obviously fears  the public reaction from this  scott griffin deputy director of the  international press institute scott we  appreciate your time and your insights  tonight thank you  thank you
 

